  "contract": [
    "Use the existing _UniqueKeyLoader as the single duplicate-key decoding owner for the23 identified authority/controller/protection/release/claim/workflow/phase mapping reads. No parallel parser, graph, registry, authority object or evaluator.",
    "Add a pure unique-document entrypoint in semantic_yaml, used by its mapping entrypoint and the existing provider consumers; preserve domain-specific top-level mapping checks, typed exceptions and supported str/bytes encodings. This has23 real consumer calls plus the existing mapping call.",
    "Duplicate explicit keys at any nesting depth, including equal-value duplicates and colliding scalar keys, reject before downstream schema/proof/planner/role selection/allocation/mutation. Supported YAML aliases and explicit merge override semantics remain valid.",
    "Keep protected source, provider identity, commit/tree inclusion, policy/evaluator separation, moving-frontier authentication, lifecycle populations and final authority independently owned. Unique YAML is parsing admission only.",
    "Validate declared Git blob OID syntax before base64 decoding or decoded-byte allocation. Preserve observed-path checks, exact blob-byte recomputation, binary/empty content and one read-only request."
  ],
  "verification": [
    "Commit contract/tests before production; retain genuine RED controls against unchanged code.",
